   1:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** /**
   2:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @file    stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c
   4:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @brief   GPIO HAL module driver.
   6:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *          This file provides firmware functions to manage the following
   7:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *          functionalities of the General Purpose Input/Output (GPIO) peripheral:
   8:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + Initialization and de-initialization functions
   9:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + IO operation functions
  10:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *
  11:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   @verbatim
  12:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  13:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****                     ##### GPIO Peripheral features #####
  14:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  15:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  16:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) Each port bit of the general-purpose I/O (GPIO) ports can be individually
  17:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         configured by software in several modes:
  18:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Input mode
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccu98KmK.s 			page 2


  19:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode
  20:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Output mode
  21:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Alternate function mode
  22:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) External interrupt/event lines
  23:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  24:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) During and just after reset, the alternate functions and external interrupt
  25:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         lines are not active and the I/O ports are configured in input floating mode.
  26:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  27:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All GPIO pins have weak internal pull-up and pull-down resistors, which can be
  28:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         activated or not.
  29:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  30:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) In Output or Alternate mode, each IO can be configured on open-drain or push-pull
  31:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         type and the IO speed can be selected depending on the VDD value.
  32:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  33:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The microcontroller IO pins are connected to onboard peripherals/modules through a
  34:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         multiplexer that allows only one peripheral alternate function (AF) connected
  35:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****        to an IO pin at a time. In this way, there can be no conflict between peripherals
  36:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****        sharing the same IO pin.
  37:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  38:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All ports have external interrupt/event capability. To use external interrupt
  39:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         lines, the port must be configured in input mode. All available GPIO pins are
  40:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         connected to the 16 external interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to EXTI15.
  41:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  42:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The external interrupt/event controller consists of up to 39 edge detectors
  43:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (16 lines are connected to GPIO) for generating event/interrupt requests (each
  44:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         input line can be independently configured to select the type (interrupt or event)
  45:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         and the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both). Each line can
  46:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         also be masked independently.
  47:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  48:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  49:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  50:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  51:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function: __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE().
  52:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  53:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  54:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Configure the IO mode using "Mode" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure
  55:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Activate Pull-up, Pull-down resistor using "Pull" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef
  56:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              structure.
  57:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of Output or alternate function mode selection: the speed is
  58:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              configured through "Speed" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  59:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In alternate mode is selection, the alternate function connected to the IO
  60:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              is configured through "Alternate" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  61:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode is required when a pin is to be used as ADC channel
  62:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              or DAC output.
  63:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of external interrupt/event selection the "Mode" member from
  64:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              GPIO_InitTypeDef structure select the type (interrupt or event) and
  65:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both).
  66:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  67:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) In case of external interrupt/event mode selection, configure NVIC IRQ priority
  68:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         mapped to the EXTI line using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority() and enable it using
  69:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  70:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  71:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use HAL_GPIO_ReadPin().
  72:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  73:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use
  74:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_GPIO_WritePin()/HAL_GPIO_TogglePin().
  75:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccu98KmK.s 			page 3


  76:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) To lock pin configuration until next reset use HAL_GPIO_LockPin().
  77:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  78:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not
  79:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except JTAG
  80:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         pins).
  81:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  82:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general purpose
  83:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE has
  84:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         priority over the GPIO function.
  85:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  86:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The HSE oscillator pins OSC_IN/OSC_OUT can be used as
  87:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         general purpose PH0 and PH1, respectively, when the HSE oscillator is off.
  88:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         The HSE has priority over the GPIO function.
  89:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  90:../../../core/ST/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   @endverbatim
